+# DNK OS Best Practices
+
+## Canvas Design
+
+### 1. Start with a Clear Goal
+- Define the main objective before creating canvas
+- Use descriptive titles (e.g., "Q4 Product Roadmap" vs "My Canvas")
+- Add tags for easy search (#roadmap, #planning, #team)
+
+### 2. Use Templates Wisely
+- **Mind Map**: Brainstorming, idea organization
+- **Flow Chart**: Process documentation, workflows
+- **Kanban**: Task management, sprint planning
+- **Timeline**: Project schedules, milestones
+
+### 3. Keep It Organized
+- Group related nodes together
+- Use consistent colors for similar items
+- Add descriptions to nodes for context
+- Limit to 20-30 nodes per canvas for clarity
+
+### 4. Collaborate Effectively
+- Share canvas with team members
+- Use comments for feedback
+- Track changes via version history
+- Set up regular sync meetings to review progress
+
+## Task Management
+
+### 1. Break Down Large Tasks
+- Split complex tasks into subtasks
+- Use SMART criteria (Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, Time-bound)
+- Assign clear owners and deadlines
+
+### 2. Prioritize Ruthlessly
+- Use Eisenhower Matrix (Urgent/Important)
+- Focus on high-impact tasks first
+- Delegate or eliminate low-priority items
+
+### 3. Review Regularly
+- Daily: Check task status
+- Weekly: Review progress, adjust priorities
